  nonce: fee8  # fee8
  message: "Fixed in PR (dev 01c9793843). Behavioral evidence on merged dev: the item's Go repro (t := source(); switch x { case 1: t = \"c\" }; sink(t)) now gives reaching definitions {(t,3,8), (t,6,8)}. Before the fix only (t,6,8) existed: the source's t never reached sink(t). The Python match twin is the same: (t,2,6) and (t,5,6). Both are in test_cfg_switch_fallthrough.py (2 passed). Fix: CfgBuilder._process_switch gives the scrutinee an always-on 'no case matched' fall-through edge. It is conservative: an exhaustive switch gains a path that never runs, which only ADDS definitions, so the walk can only refute less. WI-faful's no-recognised-arm edge is subsumed. Corpus, verify-claims vs dev: beads (Go) and feast (Python) moved no verdict, evidence count or analysis-method count. Not measured: Java/C/TS default-less switches on a corpus."  # fee8
